# DMS test-level control. Change the value below to 1 or 2; do not rename this file.
# PR/main CI and local test scripts read it. A manual workflow can override it.
#
# Level 1 (default): quick isolated regressions and provider smoke tests on all OS.
# Remote checks cover login/listing/existence/path and a small file lifecycle:
# upload/version/copy/move/download/delete, with owned setup and verified cleanup.
# Target: about 5 minutes per provider/OS; up to 8 minutes is acceptable.
# Compilation, SDK installation, reporting and queue waits are measured separately.
#
# Level 2 (cumulative): Level 1 plus extended copy/move/overwrite/failure variants,
# sharing/link/identity cases and extended isolated tests.
# Native 256 MiB/hash/active-cancellation live tests run only in a manual Level 2
# dispatch with an explicit coordinated exclusive-window end. A Level 2 push/PR
# runs the extended default-package suite; it does not grant native server access.
# Manual native_dependency_mode=packages verifies released NuGet dependencies;
# source selects the separately pinned development chain. Keep this proof distinct.
#
# Assign NUnit tests in VB (method or entire fixture):
#   <Test, Category("TestLevel1")>  - quick remote smoke test.
#   <Test, Category("TestLevel2")>  - extended remote or isolated test.
# Remote fixtures also need Category("RemoteDms") and exactly one server category,
# e.g. Category("Nextcloud"). Every remote test must resolve to exactly ONE level.
# Do not put TestLevel2 on a base fixture and TestLevel1 on its methods: inherited
# categories would select both levels. Put levels on methods for mixed fixtures.
# Isolated tests without a level category belong to Level 1; mark only slower
# isolated tests TestLevel2. Both levels always exclude RemoteDms in unlocked jobs.
# The isolated NUnit partition audit guards remote classification and base coverage.
# Server locks and complete setup/cleanup are mandatory at BOTH levels.
# See TESTING.md for commands, scope, access-window and release requirements.

TEST_LEVEL=1
